          "body_md": "**AI-assisted candidate; human review pending.**\n\nObjectives:\n- Trace pointer assignments, aliasing, and dereferencing operations on structs and heap-allocated nodes.\n- Match dynamic allocations (new / new[]) with proper deallocations (delete / delete[]) and explain ownership rules.\n- Diagnose null pointer dereferences, dangling pointers, memory leaks, and shallow-copy aliasing defects in C++.\n\nPrior knowledge: basic variables, loops, and functions. Complexity claims use constant-cost fixed-size operations unless stated otherwise. Code blocks are teaching snippets, not standalone programs. Use the external harnesses; unsafe demonstration functions must not be executed.\n\nSupporting reading (links are not approval of every claim):\n- [OpenDSA Complete Catalog — Chapter 15.1: Memory Management Introduction & Dynamic Allocation](https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/OpenDSA/Books/Catalog/html/MemmanIntro.html): Section 15.1: Dynamic Memory Allocation, Heap Free Store, and Pointer Lifetimes\n- [Open Data Structures (in C++) — Preface to the C++ Edition & Chapter 2: Array-Based Lists (Backing Array Allocation)](https://opendatastructures.org/ods-cpp/Preface_C_Edition.html): Preface to the C++ Edition (C++ Pointers, Templates, and Manual Memory Management vs STL)"
