          "body_md": "Calling `pop()` or `top()` on an empty stack invokes Stack Underflow. In raw C++ implementations using unchecked array buffers, this results in an out-of-bounds negative index dereference (`data[-1]`), causing memory corruption or segmentation faults. Always verify `!st.empty()` prior to pop or top."
