          "title": "Deep Dive: Gauss's Proof of the Sum of First n Integers",
          "body_md": "Young Carl Friedrich Gauss proved $\\sum_{i=1}^n i = \\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$ by writing the sum twice—once forward and once backward. Pairing terms $(1 + n) + (2 + n - 1) + \\dots + (n + 1)$ creates $n$ pairs, each summing to $(n + 1)$, yielding $2S = n(n + 1)$."
