          "prompt": "If algorithm A has runtime $O(n^2)$ and algorithm B has runtime $O(n)$, does algorithm B always run faster than algorithm A for every input?",
          "reveal_md": "No. Big-O characterizes asymptotic behavior as n approaches infinity. For small inputs (e.g. n < 10), algorithm A with a small constant (e.g. $0.01 n^2$) can run significantly faster than algorithm B with a large constant (e.g. 1000 n).",
