          "body_md": "Average-case analysis averages runtimes over an assumed probability distribution of inputs. In contrast, **Amortized Analysis** guarantees the average cost per operation over ANY arbitrary sequence of $n$ operations in the worst case, without making probabilistic assumptions (e.g. dynamic vector doubling)."
