      "stem": "Suppose you are given only a pointer `Node* v` to an interior node (guaranteed `v != nullptr` and `v->next != nullptr`, so `v` is NOT the tail) in a singly linked list, with no access to `head`. How can you delete the logical element at `v` in $O(1)$ time, and why does this trick fail if `v` is the tail node?",
