      "stem": "An open-addressing hash table uses linear probing. Each slot is `EMPTY`, `OCCUPIED`, or `DELETED` (a tombstone left behind by a removal). Keys are unique, and the table always keeps at least one `EMPTY` slot. How should (1) `search(k)` and (2) `insert(k)` treat a `DELETED` slot they meet while probing?",
