      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "Substituting `alpha = 0.5` gives `0.5 * (1 + 1 / 0.25) = 0.5 * 5 = 2.5` probes. Substituting `alpha = 0.9` gives `0.5 * (1 + 1 / 0.01) = 0.5 * 101 = 50.5` probes. Performance degrades rapidly once `alpha > 0.5` due to primary clustering.",
