      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "In hash table probe analysis, random/uniform probing requires `1 / (1 - alpha) = 10` expected probes at `alpha = 0.9`. In contrast, linear probing suffers from primary clustering and requires $0.5 \\cdot (1 + 1 / (1 - \\alpha)^2) = 0.5 \\cdot (1 + 100) = 50.5$ probes—over 5 times more work. At `alpha = 0.5`, the difference is modest (2.0 vs 2.5 probes).",
