      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "What is the time complexity of the following conditional function on an array `A` of size `n`?\n```cpp\nvoid process(std::vector<int>& A) {\n    if (A.size() % 2 == 0) {\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < A.size(); ++i) A[i] += 1; // Theta(n)\n    } else {\n        for (size_t i = 0; i < A.size(); ++i)\n            for (size_t j = 0; j < A.size(); ++j)\n                A[i] += A[j]; // Theta(n^2)\n    }\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "Overall worst-case time is $\\Theta(n)$ because exactly half of all positive integers are even and take the fast linear branch."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "Worst-case time is $\\Theta(n^3)$ because the $\\Theta(n)$ `if`-branch and the $\\Theta(n^2)$ `else`-branch must be multiplied together across all inputs."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "Best-case time is $\\Theta(n)$ (even `n`), Worst-case is $\\Theta(n^2)$ (odd `n`), so overall worst-case is $O(n^2)$ with no single $\\Theta(n^k)$ bound."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "Both best-case and worst-case time are $\\Theta(n^2)$."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "C",
      "answer_explanation": "For an `if-else` statement where the condition takes $O(1)$, a single execution runs *either* the `if` branch ($\\Theta(n)$) *or* the `else` branch ($\\Theta(n^2)$), never both. Thus worst-case time is $\\max(\\Theta(n), \\Theta(n^2)) = \\Theta(n^2)$ (on odd `n`) and best-case time is $\\Theta(n)$ (on even `n`).",
