      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "Suppose a dynamic array grows by adding a fixed constant `K = 100` slots (`capacity += 100`) whenever it is full, rather than doubling (`capacity *= 2`). What is the total time complexity of performing `n` consecutive `push_back` operations starting from an empty array, and what is the resulting amortized cost per `push_back`?",
