          "text": "Total time is $\\Theta(n^2)$ and amortized cost per `push_back` degrades to $\\Theta(n)$ since reallocations occur at sizes `100, 200, 300,..., n`, copying $100 \\cdot (1 + 2 +\\dots + n/100) = \\Theta(n^2)$ elements in total."
