      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Arithmetic capacity growth (`+K`) triggers `n / K` resizes whose copy costs form an arithmetic series $K + 2K + 3K + \\dots + n = \\Theta(n^2 / K) = \\Theta(n^2)$. Dividing by `n` operations yields $\\Theta(n)$ amortized time per `push_back`. Geometric growth (`* 2`) is mandatory to form a geometric series summing to $O(n)$ ($O(1)$ amortized).",
