      "stem": "In an unsorted array `A[0 .. n-1]` of `n` distinct elements, suppose the searched key `x` is guaranteed to be in `A` and is equally likely to be at any of the `n` indices (`probability 1/n` each). What are the best-case, worst-case, and average-case numbers of key comparisons (`A[i] == x`) performed by standard Linear Search?",
