      "answer_explanation": "Iterative Linear Search uses only a single loop index variable `i` ($O(1)$ auxiliary space). Without tail-call optimization, recursive Linear Search pushes a stack frame for each index `i = 0, 1, ..., n`, consuming $\\Theta(n)$ call-stack space in the worst case.",
