      "answer_explanation": "Under C++17 (`[expr]/4`), signed integer overflow in `low + high` when `low + high > INT_MAX` (`2,147,483,647`) is Undefined Behavior (on typical two's-complement targets it wraps to a negative value and indexes `A[mid]` out of bounds). When `0 <= low <= high`, `high - low` stays in `[0, high]` and cannot overflow.",
