      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "A student writes Binary Search with a closed interval `[low, high]` as:\n```cpp\nint bsearchBug(const std::vector<int>& A, int key) {\n    int low = 0, high = static_cast<int>(A.size()) - 1;\n    while (low <= high) {\n        int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;\n        if (A[mid] == key) return mid;\n        if (A[mid] < key) low = mid;      // <-- Note this line\n        else high = mid - 1;\n    }\n    return -1;\n}\n```\nWhat happens when calling `bsearchBug({10, 20}, 20)` (or searching for `25` in `{10, 20}`)?",
