      "stem": "In Binary Insertion Sort, we use Binary Search on the sorted prefix `A[0 .. i-1]` to find the insertion index for `A[i]` in $O(\\log i)$ comparisons, and then shift the elements in `A[pos .. i-1]` right by one slot. How does this affect the worst-case number of comparisons and the worst-case total running time on a contiguous array?",
