      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "Why does standard Insertion Sort save `int key = A[i];` and shift elements right (`A[j + 1] = A[j]`) before writing `A[j + 1] = key` once at the end of the inner loop, rather than calling `std::swap(A[j], A[j + 1])` on every inner-loop step?",
