      "answer_explanation": "When `maxIdx == left`, the element at `left` is the maximum. Executing `swap(A[left], A[minIdx])` first relocates the maximum from `left` to `minIdx`. If `maxIdx` is not updated to `minIdx` before executing `swap(A[right], A[maxIdx])`, the second swap pulls the newly placed minimum out of `A[left]` and puts it at `A[right]`.",
