      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "Consider the buggy recursive function intended to test if a non-negative integer `n` is even:\n```cpp\nbool isEvenBug(int n) {\n    if (n == 0) return true;\n    return isEvenBug(n - 2);\n}\n```\nWhat happens when `isEvenBug(5)` is called?",
