      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "Consider eliminating recursion from a divide-and-conquer array partition routine `sortRange(A, low, high)` (such as Quick Sort), which splits `[low..high]` at index `p` into `[low..p-1]` and `[p+1..high]`. How do we guarantee $O(\\log n)$ worst-case auxiliary stack space even when splits are maximally uneven?",
