      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "A student writes the following recursive function to test whether a binary tree (with distinct keys) is a valid Binary Search Tree (BST):\n```cpp\nbool isBSTLocalBug(Node* r) {\n    if (!r) return true;\n    if (r->left && r->left->key >= r->key) return false;\n    if (r->right && r->right->key <= r->key) return false;\n    return isBSTLocalBug(r->left) && isBSTLocalBug(r->right);\n}\n```\nWhy is `isBSTLocalBug` incorrect, and which 3-vertex tree is a counterexample where it falsely returns `true`?",
