      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "In a Binary Search Tree, suppose node `u` has two non-null children (`u->left != nullptr` and `u->right != nullptr`), and we want to delete `u` using Hibbard Deletion (`ACT_C10_01`). Which two nodes in the tree can validly replace `u`'s key while preserving the global BST invariant, and how many children can that replacement node have at its original position?",
