      "stem": "Why are B-Trees (and B+ Trees) with high branching factors (`t = 100` to `500`, where one B-tree node equals one `4 KB – 16 KB` disk/SSD page) universally used for database and filesystem indexes instead of AVL or Red-Black binary search trees?",
