      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "In top-down `B-Tree-Delete` (parameterized by minimum degree `t`), why does the downward search ensure that every child node `y` it descends into has at least `t` keys (at least 1 key *more* than the minimum `t - 1`) before recursing into `y`?",
