      "question_category": "tracing_application",
      "stem": "In a B-Tree of minimum degree `t = 3` (`minimum t - 1 = 2 keys`, `maximum 2t - 1 = 5 keys`), suppose parent node `x` has key `50` separating two adjacent children `y` (left) and `z` (right), where both `y` and `z` currently have the minimum `t - 1 = 2` keys (`y = [10, 20]` and `z = [60, 70]`). When `y` and `z` are merged around `50`, how many keys does the merged node contain, and why does this fit cleanly into a single node?",
