      "answer_explanation": "This is why the standard B-tree capacity bounds `[t - 1, 2t - 1]` are so mathematically clean: two minimal nodes (`t - 1` keys each) plus `1` separator key from the parent combine into `(t - 1) + 1 + (t - 1) = 2t - 1` keys, fitting perfectly into one maximal node.",
