      "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
      "stem": "Suppose a database table is empty and we have `N = 10,000,000` records already sorted by primary key to load into a B-Tree / B+ Tree index. Why do database systems use a specialized Bulk-Loading algorithm rather than calling standard `insert(k)` `N` times one by one?",
