      "learning_objective_id": "T11_1_LO1",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "By a direct corollary of the Handshaking Lemma (`sum_{v in V} deg(v) = 2|E|`), in any finite undirected graph `G = (V, E)`, what must always be true about the number of vertices that have an odd degree?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "The number of vertices with an odd degree is always even (possibly `0`)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "The number of vertices with an odd degree equals the number of connected components."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "The number of vertices with an even degree is always even."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "If `|E|` is odd, the number of odd-degree vertices must be odd."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "Split `V` into `V_even` and `V_odd`. Since `sum_{v in V_even} deg(v) + sum_{v in V_odd} deg(v) = 2|E|` is even, and `sum_{v in V_even} deg(v)` is a sum of even integers (hence even), the sum `sum_{v in V_odd} deg(v)` of odd integers must also be even—which requires `|V_odd|` to be an even integer.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "B": "A single tree `K_2` (1 component) has 2 odd-degree vertices; a cycle `C_3` (1 component) has 0 odd-degree vertices.",
        "C": "`|V_even|` has the same parity as `|V|`, which can be odd (e.g., `K_3` has 3 vertices all of even degree 2).",
        "D": "`2|E|` is even even when `|E|` is odd. For example, `K_3` has `|E| = 3` (odd) and `0` (even) odd-degree vertices."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "hard",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "MC_ODD_DEGREE_VERTICES_PARITY"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graph_(discrete_mathematics)#Definitions",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handshaking_lemma"
      ],
      "verification_method": "symbolic_check",
