      "learning_objective_id": "T11_1_LO3",
      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "In a directed graph `G = (V, E)`, consider the relation `u ~ v` defined by '`u` and `v` are mutually reachable' (there is a directed path from `u` to `v` and from `v` to `u`, with `u ~ u` via a path of length 0). If we contract each equivalence class (Strongly Connected Component, SCC) into a single super-vertex, what kind of graph is the resulting component graph $G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "$G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ is always a strongly connected graph."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "$G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ is always a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG)."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "$G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ is always an undirected tree."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "$G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ may contain directed cycles if the original graph `G` had nested cycles."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "B",
      "answer_explanation": "Suppose $G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ had a directed cycle of distinct super-vertices `C_1 -> C_2 -> ... -> C_k -> C_1` (`k >= 2`). Then every vertex in `C_1` could reach every vertex in `C_2` and vice versa, meaning `C_1` and `C_2` would be mutually reachable and thus belong to the *same* SCC—a contradiction. Hence $G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ is always a DAG.",
      "distractor_explanations": {
        "A": "If $G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ has `>= 2` vertices, it has no cycles and therefore cannot be strongly connected.",
        "C": "$G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$ is a directed acyclic graph (which may have multiple paths between super-vertices, such as a diamond DAG, not necessarily a tree).",
        "D": "Nested cycles in `G` share vertices or mutual reachability and merge into a *single* SCC super-vertex in $G^{\\mathrm{SCC}}$."
      },
      "difficulty_estimate": "hard",
      "misconception_tags": [
        "MC_SCC_CONDENSATION_IS_DAG"
      ],
      "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
      "reference_sources": [
        "https://opendsa-server.cs.vt.edu/OpenDSA/Books/CS3/html/GraphIntro.html#graph-terminology-and-implementation",
        "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strongly_connected_component"
      ],
