      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "An Adjacency Matrix always allocates a `V x V` table of entries regardless of how few edges exist ($\\Theta(V^2)$ space). An Adjacency List allocates an array of `V` vertex headers plus one node per directed edge (`E` total) or two per undirected edge (`2E` total), yielding $\\Theta(V + E)$ space.",
