      "stem": "A student builds a `V x V` Adjacency Matrix for weighted shortest-path computations using:\n```cpp\nstd::vector<std::vector<int>> mat(V, std::vector<int>(V, 0));\n```\nWhy is initializing `mat[u][v] = 0` for `u != v` a bug, and what is the standard convention?",
