      "stem": "Suppose you are given a directed graph `G = (V, E)` stored ONLY as an outgoing Adjacency List `adj[u]` (which lists all `v` such that `(u, v) in E`). What is the time complexity to compute the out-degree $\\deg^+(w)$ of a single vertex `w` vs computing the in-degree $\\deg^-(w)$ of that single vertex `w` (without precomputed in-degrees)?",
