      "answer_explanation": "Using a hash table per vertex (`std::vector<std::unordered_set<int>>`) stores only existing edges ($\\Theta(V + E)$ total entries) while supporting expected $O(1)$ lookup and deletion of `(u, v)`. However, hash buckets have larger constant-factor memory overhead and poorer spatial locality during BFS/DFS scans than `std::vector<int>`.",
