      "stem": "Why does a standard FIFO-queue BFS fail to guarantee shortest paths when edges have non-uniform positive weights (for example, triangle `0 -> 1` with weight `10`, `0 -> 2` with weight `2`, and `2 -> 1` with weight `3`), and why does it work on unweighted graphs?",
