        "B": "`std::queue` can hold any C++ type, including `std::pair<int, int>`; the issue is FIFO ordering vs min-distance ordering.",
        "C": "As shown by the counterexample `w(0,1)=10 > w(0,2)+w(2,1)=2+3=5`, BFS fails as soon as a 2-edge path is lighter than a 1-edge path."
