      "stem": "Suppose we want to convert recursive `DFS(0)` into an iterative DFS using an explicit `std::stack<int> S` so that it visits vertices in the exact same discovery order as recursive DFS (which explores `adj[u]` from index `0` to `adj[u].size() - 1`). If we push all unvisited neighbors of `u` onto `S` when `u` is popped, in what order must we push `adj[u]` onto the LIFO stack `S`?",
