      "stem": "In an undirected connected graph `G = (V, E)`, a vertex `u` is an articulation point (cut vertex) if removing `u` disconnects `G`, and an edge `e` is a bridge if removing `e` disconnects `G`. In Tarjan's $O(V + E)$ DFS algorithm, what information does `low[u]` track to identify bridges and articulation points?",
