      "stem": "Consider a directed path graph `0 -> 1 -> 2 -> ... -> (V - 1)` with `V = 200,000` vertices. Why can a naive recursive C++ implementation of `DFS(0)` crash with a Segmentation Fault (`SIGSEGV`) on this valid sparse graph in some grading environments, and how is it prevented?",
