      "question_category": "complexity_analysis",
      "stem": "In Kruskal's Algorithm on a graph with `V` vertices and `E` edges, why do we use the Disjoint Set Union (DSU / Union-Find) data structure with path compression and union by rank/size, and what is the resulting overall time complexity of Kruskal's algorithm?",
