      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "Given two strings `X` of length `m` and `Y` of length `n` whose Longest Common Subsequence has length `L = LCS(X, Y)`, what are the exact formulas for:\n1. The minimum number of character deletions and insertions (Edit Distance without substitutions) needed to transform `X` into `Y`?\n2. The length of the Shortest Common Supersequence (SCS) (the shortest string `Z` that contains both `X` and `Y` as subsequences)?",
