      "learning_objective_id": "T14_1_LO2",
      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Why does the standard Greedy Coin-Changing algorithm (repeatedly picking the largest coin denomination `c <= remaining_amount`) always find the minimum number of coins for standard US/VN currency (`{1, 5, 10, 25}`), yet FAIL for non-canonical coin systems such as `coins = {1, 7, 10}` with target `S = 14`?",
