      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "In Metric TSP, direct edges are at least as short as detours (`d(u, v) <= d(u, w) + d(w, v)`). Taking a full DFS walk of the MST uses each of the `n - 1` MST edges twice (once down, once up), costing `2 * w(MST) <= 2 * OPT_TSP`. Converting this walk into a Hamiltonian cycle by skipping repeated vertices in preorder replaces multi-edge paths with direct edges, which by the Triangle Inequality costs `<= 2 * w(MST) <= 2 * OPT_TSP`.",
