      "stem": "Suppose directed edge `(u, v) in E` has capacity `c(u, v) = 12` and currently carries flow `f(u, v) = 9` (with no antiparallel edge `(v, u)` in `E`). In the residual network `G_f`, what are `c_f(u, v)` and `c_f(v, u)`, and if an augmenting path pushes `Delta = 4` units of flow along the backward residual edge `(v, u)`, what becomes the new flow `f'(u, v)` and new residual capacities `c_{f'}(u, v)` and `c_{f'}(v, u)`?",
