      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "In a flow network `G = (V, E)` with source `s` and sink `t`, what is an `s-t` cut `(S, T)`, and how are the capacity of the cut `c(S, T)` and the net flow across the cut `f(S, T)` defined?",
