      "correct_option_id": "D",
      "answer_explanation": "Memorize this essential asymmetry between Cut Capacity and Net Flow across a Cut:\n- Cut Capacity `c(S, T)`: sums `c(u, v)` ONLY for forward edges `u in S -> v in T` (edges pointing backward from `T` to `S` do NOT add to nor subtract from `c(S, T)`.).\n- Net Flow `f(S, T)`: equals forward flow (`S -> T`) MINUS backward flow (`T -> S`).",
