      "concept_id": "C15",
      "topic_id": "T15_1",
      "learning_objective_id": "T15_1_LO3",
      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Consider a flow network with `V = {s, a, b, t}` and cut `(S = {s, a}, T = {b, t})`. Suppose the edges crossing between `S` and `T` are:\n- `a -> b`: capacity `c(a, b) = 10`, current flow `f(a, b) = 8` (`S -> T`)\n- `s -> b`: capacity `c(s, b) = 5`, current flow `f(s, b) = 4` (`S -> T`)\n- `b -> a`: capacity `c(b, a) = 7`, current flow `f(b, a) = 3` (`T -> S`.)\nWhat are the exact cut capacity `c(S, T)` and the net flow `f(S, T)` across this cut?",
      "options": [
        {
          "option_id": "A",
          "text": "`c(S, T) = 10 + 5 = 15`, and `f(S, T) = (8 + 4) - 3 = 9`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "B",
          "text": "`c(S, T) = 10 + 5 + 7 = 22` and `f(S, T) = 8 + 4 + 3 = 15`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "C",
          "text": "`c(S, T) = (10 + 5) - 7 = 8` and `f(S, T) = (8 + 4) - 3 = 9`."
        },
        {
          "option_id": "D",
          "text": "`c(S, T) = 15` and `f(S, T) = 8 + 4 = 12`."
        }
      ],
      "correct_option_id": "A",
      "answer_explanation": "Apply the definitions directly:\n1. Forward edges (`u in S = {s, a}`, `v in T = {b, t}`) are `(a, b)` and `(s, b)`, so `c(S, T) = c(a, b) + c(s, b) = 10 + 5 = 15`.\n2. Backward edge (`v in T, u in S`) is `(b, a)` with `f(b, a) = 3`, so `f(S, T) = (f(a, b) + f(s, b)) - f(b, a) = (8 + 4) - 3 = 9` (and notice `|f| = f(S, T) = 9 <= 15 = c(S, T)`.).",
