      "question_category": "concept_invariant",
      "stem": "By Menger's Theorem (Edge-Connectivity version), in a directed (or undirected) graph `G = (V, E)`, if we assign every edge in `E` a unit capacity `c(u, v) = 1` and run Maximum Flow from `s` to `t`, what two graph-theoretic quantities equal the resulting maximum flow value $|f^*|$?",
