      "question_category": "code_trace",
      "stem": "Conversely, suppose we have an integer Maximum Flow $f^*$ in `G`, and an edge `e = (u, v)` currently carrying positive flow $f^*(u, v) \\ge 1$ has its capacity decreased by `-1` (`c'(u, v) = c(u, v) - 1`). If $f^*(u, v)$ was equal to `c(u, v)` (so $f^*$ now violates the new capacity `c'(u, v)` by `1` unit), how can we restore a valid Maximum Flow in $O(V + E)$ time without recomputing Max-Flow from zero?",
