          "learning_objective_id": "T08_2_LO3",
          "question_category": "edge_cases_complexity",
          "stem": "Does the C++17 language standard guarantee that every C++ compiler will perform Tail-Call Optimization (TCO) on all tail-recursive functions (even in debug builds `-O0` or when local objects have non-trivial destructors)?",
          "options": [
            {
              "option_id": "A",
              "text": "Yes; the C++17 standard mandates tail-call elimination in all build modes (including `-O0` debug builds) even when local objects have non-trivial destructors."
            },
            {
              "option_id": "B",
              "text": "No; C++17 does not mandate TCO, and local objects with non-trivial destructors run after the call returns. An explicit loop guarantees $O(1)$ stack space."
            },
            {
              "option_id": "C",
              "text": "No C++ compiler is capable of performing TCO even at `-O2`."
            },
            {
              "option_id": "D",
              "text": "Destructors in C++ always execute *before* the `return` expression is evaluated."
            }
          ],
          "correct_option_id": "B",
          "answer_explanation": "In C++, local objects with automatic storage duration are destroyed *after* the return expression is evaluated. Thus a local `std::vector` or `std::string` inside a 'tail-recursive' C++ function adds hidden post-call destructor work. Additionally, debug builds (`-O0`) disable TCO to preserve stack traces. Explicitly transforming tail recursion into a `while` loop guarantees $O(1)$ stack space unconditionally.",
          "distractor_explanations": {
            "A": "Unlike Scheme (which mandates proper tail calls in its specification), C++ leaves TCO as an optional compiler optimization.",
            "C": "GCC, Clang, and MSVC all perform TCO at `-O2` when no non-trivial destructors remain active after the call.",
            "D": "Local destructors run when exiting the block scope, *after* the `return fn(...)` call completes."
          },
          "difficulty_estimate": "medium",
          "misconception_tags": [
            "cpp_tco_non_trivial_destructor_caveat"
          ],
          "authorship_type": "AI-assisted team-authored",
          "reference_sources": [
            "https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/return#Explanation",
            "https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/destructor#Explanation",
            "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail_call#Language_support",
            "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tail_call#Hardware_and_space_complexity",
            "https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/Optimize-Options.html#index-foptimize-sibling-calls",
            "https://clang.llvm.org/docs/AttributeReference.html#musttail"
          ],
          "verification_method": "source_cross_check",
          "agent_check_status": "passed",
          "human_review_status": "pending",
          "approved_by": null,
          "approved_at": null,
